==Battleground==
*1 [[Filibuster Obstructa]] spawns as the boss after 1.67 seconds<sup>50f</sup>.
*1 [[Bun Bun Symbiote]] spawns as the boss after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Bore]] spawns as the boss after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*1 [[Shadow Boxer K]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*1 [[Kid Tappa]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 50% HP:
**1 [[General GreGory]] spawns as the boss.
*When the base reaches 25% HP:
**1 [[General GreGory]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Since Filibuster Obstructa will destroy the [[Cat Base]] in one hit regardless of where his attack fires off, you'll have to prevent him from ever completing his 40-second attack animation.

Filibuster spawns with a Kid Tappa, which can be ignored, as he doesn't do much damage to the Cat Base. Due to how [[Long Distance]] works, you should not try to spawn any cat units until Filibuster is close enough to the [[Cat Base]], as while his standing range is truly massive, his minimum range is only 300. You can wait for him to almost complete his attack animation before spawning [[Courier Cat]] or other [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cats]] to knock him back, then wait some more to ensure you have more than enough money. Once enough money is accumulated, summon [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] along with other cats that are effective against [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]]. Don't focus on [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]], as he is immune to [[Wave Attack]]s (which also means the [[Cat Cannon]] can't reset his attack animation), and don't bother with [[:Category:Cats with Warp Immunity|Cats with Warp Immunity]], as none of the enemies here can warp. You can, however, use [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attackers]] (e.g. talented [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]]), as while they are uncommon and tend to be inconsistent, Filibuster isn't immune to [[Surge Attack]]s. Just beware that Filibuster usually won't move forward again once he's knocked back due to your units approaching him.

After dispatching Kid Tappa, several enemies will spawn one by one (due to the enemy limit of 2) to assist Filibuster Obstructa, including Bun Bun Symbiote, Shadow Boxer K and a Bore. They largely function as meatshields for Filibuster Obstructa and players must build an effective multi-purpose lineup to deal with these threats before Filibuster finishes his attack animation. [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Megaphrodite]] and [[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Hayabusa]] are excellent [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] for this stage, while [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]] would be the most effective [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rares]]. Once all these enemies are down, Filibuster is no longer a threat due to his absurdly high KB count, and can be easily finished off, as with the General GreGories spawned upon hitting the enemy base.

[[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] is very effective against Filibuster Obstructa, as it's able to continuously interrupt its attacks, granted it doesn't hit the enemy in front.

If you have [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] and [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]], it's a good idea to use both of them in this stage, because not only do they prevent Shadow Boxer K and Bore from easily defeating your units, but they make killing them a LOT easier, allowing your units to safely chip away Filibuster's health. [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] and [[Swordsman Cat (Rare Cat)|Elemental Duelist Cat]]/[[Courier Cat]] also find themselves useful against Shadow Boxer K and Bore.

